# UI-Finder — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to a new file named `.env.local` in the same folder, fill
# in real values, then restart `npm run dev` (or redeploy).
# `.env.local` is already git-ignored — never commit real keys.
#
# All three services below are required for the real pipeline to run.
# Without them the app still loads, but "Find Similar UI" will stop at
# the step that needs the missing key and tell you exactly which one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Google Gemini — understands the submitted UI (structure, layout,
#    columns, tabs, cards, hierarchy) and later compares it against
#    candidate website sections.
#
#    How to get one (free, no credit card):
#    1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com
#    2. Click "Get API key" -> "Create API key".
#    3. Copy the key and paste it below.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override which Gemini model is used. Needs multimodal
# (image) input and JSON-schema structured output support.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Exa Search — discovers real webpages that might contain a similar
#    UI section, using the structural search queries Gemini generates.
#
#    How to get one: https://exa.ai -> sign up -> API Keys.
EXA_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Browserbase — opens each candidate webpage in a real, remote
#    browser, inspects its DOM structure, and captures section
#    screenshots. UI-Finder connects to it over CDP (playwright-core),
#    so no local Chromium install is needed.
#
#    How to get these: https://www.browserbase.com -> sign up ->
#    grab your API key and Project ID from the dashboard.
BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=
BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID=
